}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/kibana/deployments","created_at":"2013-01-26T04:00:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T08:25:14Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-09T08:35:08Z","git_url":"git://github.com/elastic/kibana.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:elastic/kibana.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/elastic/kibana.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/elastic/kibana","homepage":"https://www.elastic.co/products/kibana","size":13528761,"stargazers_count":20989,"watchers_count":20989,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":8541,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":13148,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["dashboards","elasticsearch","hacktoberfest","kibana","metrics","observability","visualizations"],"visibility":"public","forks":8541,"open_issues":13148,"watchers":20989,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I am opening this as a follow-up to https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/21977. The described bug could be fixed by formatting the field so what appears today as garbage would be properly formatted as an ip address. This will also format the date field, based on the format that is defined in the mappings. I have vague memories that Kibana may have used `docvalue_fields` in the past to get dates back as numbers of millis since Epoch, in which case the bug fix would break Kibana. So is it the case? If that is still a requirement for Kibana then one way to fix it would be to give the ability to define a format alongside each field, like for aggregations, so that passing eg. `epoch_millis` as a format would 